### Skill Trigger Matrix

> If you think there is even a 1% chance a skill applies to what you are doing, you MUST use it. This is not optional and cannot be rationalized away.
> **If your agent has no skill-loading mechanism**: skills are plain Markdown — read `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` directly and follow it (e.g. `.agents/skills/clarify/SKILL.md` as the Stage-01 clarification protocol).

| What you are doing | Skill to use | Key principle |
|--------------------|--------------|---------------|
| Starting a requirement / the user describes a change | `devsop.init` (once per project) + `clarify` (per task, Stage 01) | Scaffold first; clarify before plan |
| Planning / implementing / committing any task | The 9-step DEVSOP below (per-task md artifacts, TDD red-green) | Evidence in `.docs/plans/<task>/` |
| Baseline or monthly compliance check | `devsop.eval` (supports `--dry-run` / `--only` / `--diff-from`) | Measure before you judge |
| Reviewing incremental changes for secrets (any language) | `secret-leak-review` | Diff-scoped, read-only, L0-L4 levels |
| Writing a new project skill | `devsop.skill-authoring` | Anatomy + verification + no tool lock-in |

### Three-Tier Boundaries

| Tier | Meaning | Examples (extend per project) |
|------|---------|-------------------------------|
| ✅ Always do | Non-negotiable defaults | Run lint+UT before commit; write per-stage md artifacts; follow `.docs/coding-style.md` |
| ⚠️ Ask first | Higher-risk or user-preference-dependent | Hot-deploying to the test environment (Stage 05); changing public API; adding a dependency |
| 🚫 Never do | Hard prohibitions | Commit secrets/credentials; skip TDD red-green; modify other tasks' md artifacts; `git push --force` (use `--force-with-lease`) |

