## §2 DEVSOP (Standard Development Flow)

> **Trigger**: when the user describes a requirement / says "start DEVSOP" / "create a task: <description>", enter automatically, advancing from Step 1 Clarify.
> **Entry determination**: after establishing/locating the task directory, if `01-clarify.md` already has valid content → skip Clarify and go directly to Plan (requires user confirmation + mark the skip in `00-overview.md`).

### Context Recovery (MANDATORY every session / clear / compact)

> <EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>
> This recovery protocol is non-negotiable. Skipping it because "I remember this project" is forbidden — state changes between sessions, and stale context corrupts the current task.
> </EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>
>
> 1. Read `AGENTS.md` → 2. `git branch --show-current` → 3. Traverse `.docs/plans/*/00-overview.md` to match the branch → 4. Read the current task's `00-overview.md` → 5. Lazy-load the current stage md → 6. Report progress to the user.
> No match → handle per the "DEVSOP Startup Prerequisites".

### Task Isolation (mandatory)

> **Strictly forbidden** for AI to proactively read/reference any md under **other** task directories `.docs/plans/<other task>/`. Tasks are physically isolated and each is an independent source of truth; cross-task references will contaminate design judgment.
> **The only exception**: the user **explicitly** says "reference task X" → read only the specified directory; the content stays in the conversation context, and **writing back to the current task's deliverables automatically is forbidden**.

### DEVSOP Startup Prerequisites: Branch and Task Determination

> 1. `git branch --show-current` to get the branch name
> 2. Match the branch under `.docs/plans/`:
>    - **Has a matching task** → continue per `00-overview.md`
>    - **None + on master/main** → brand-new requirement: `git checkout -b feature/<name> origin/master` → `cp -r .docs/plans/_template .docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD_<title>` → **simplify the comments** (see ③ below) → fill in Meta → enter the entry determination
>    - **None + on a feature/ branch** → "Collaborative Development Detection"
> 3. **After copying _template/, the comments must be simplified** (applies to brand-new requirements / collaborative development, **AI must execute**): open the new `plans/<task>/00-overview.md`, delete **entirely** all HTML comment blocks marked with `<!-- TEMPLATE-ONLY-DO-NOT-COPY: -->` (including the marker lines), replacing them with a single-line pointer to `_template/00-overview.md`; also delete **entirely** the header "⚠️ TEMPLATE ONLY" section. DEVSOP rules are maintained only in `_template/`; it is **forbidden** to repeat ~30 lines of rules in every task file (noise + version drift). See the top of `_template/00-overview.md` for details.
>
> **Forbidden** to do DEVSOP on `master`/`main`; one branch may only correspond to one task directory.

### Collaborative Development Detection (design.md-driven)

> Trigger: current branch is non-master/main and has no matching task.
> - `.docs/design.md` exists and the user confirms using it → create the task directory (also simplify _template/ comments per ③ above) → fully derive `01-clarify.md` + `02-plan.md` from design.md (forbidden to just write "see design.md") → fill in Meta (`Development mode`=collaborative, `Test environment`) → after self-check, delete design.md → start from Step 3
> - design.md does not exist → standard flow

### The 9 Step Definitions

| # | Step | Deliverable | Description |
|---|------|------|------|
| 1 | **Clarify** | `01-clarify.md` | `skill: clarify` clarifies the requirements, producing background/goals/open questions |
| 2 | **Plan** | `02-plan.md` | Changed files, call chain, **§6 UT cases (TDD required)**, IT cases, risks |
| 3 | **Implement** | `03-implement.md` | Red-Green cycle per Plan §6: write UT and run red first → minimal implementation to green → refactor |
| 4 | **UT** | `04-ut.md` | Cases aligned item by item with Plan §6, coverage, uncovered lines |
| 5 | **Deploy** | `05-deploy.md` | Hot-deploy code to the test environment via the team environment management Skill |
| 6 | **IT** | `06-it.md` | Paste key logs (with reqid) for each case; not skipped in collaborative mode |
| 7 | **Docs** | `07-docs.md` | Incrementally update `.docs/` |
| 8 | **Review** | `08-review.md` | Code review results |
| 9 | **Commit** | `09-commit.md` | ① Ask about the issue/task ticket → ② Release the environment → ③ Advance the ticket status to "Developing" → ④ Write commit message → ⑤ Update overview (boundary point A) → ⑥ One-time `git add` → ⑦ `git commit` (first time only) → ⑧ `git push` creates the MR, triggering the ticket status "Developing→CR" → ⑨ (repeatable until the MR merges) amend to accumulate fixes (one MR one commit principle) |

### Task Size Branch

> **Trigger condition**: when the 02 Plan stage estimates `estimated code change lines ≤ 10`, set `Small-requirement mode` to ✅ in the `00-overview.md` Meta. From 03 onward, execute per the rules below.

| # | Step | Standard Mode | Small-Requirement Mode |
|---|------|----------|------------|
| 1 | Clarify  | Confirm | **Confirm** |
| 2 | Plan     | Confirm | **Confirm** |
| 3 | Implement | Confirm | **Automatic** (run combined with 04, report once at the end) |
| 4 | UT       | Confirm | **Automatic** (run combined with 03, report once at the end) |
| 5 | Deploy   | Confirm | **Confirm** (environment-sensitive, must be explicitly confirmed) |
| 6 | IT       | Confirm | **Confirm** (involves real chain / reqid verification, skipping confirmation is not allowed) |
| 7 | Docs     | Confirm | **Automatic** |
| 8 | Review   | Confirm | **Automatic** |
| 9 | Commit   | Confirm | **Automatic** (environment release still follows section 0 of `09-commit.md`) |

> "Automatic" ≠ skip deliverables: the md deliverables of 03-04 / 07-09, the `00-overview.md` time records, and Progress check-offs **must still** be written per the normal flow. "Automatic" only means merging the two confirmations (start/end) of the step into one — AI says "I'm going to do X-Y-Z" once and starts running, then reports once at the end ("03-04 complete (summary of conclusions)"), **without interrupting the user in between**.
>
> **05 Deploy / 06 IT must still be explicitly confirmed**: Deploy involves environment side effects and IT involves real-chain verification; these are the two most error-prone steps in the DEVSOP and are not included in the automatic batch.
>
> **Batch time records**: for the 03-04 / 07-09 batches, the `00-overview.md` time-tracking table writes the **same** start time and the **same** end time for every row of each batch (the moment the batch starts/ends), and the duration is also the same value; write "Small-requirement mode batch: 03-04" or "Small-requirement mode batch: 07-09" in the remarks column for aggregation. See rule 9 of the `00-overview.md` time-tracking section.
>
> **Rollback mechanism**: if, after entering 03, the actual changes turn out > 10 lines (underestimate), AI should change `Small-requirement mode` back to ⬜ when reporting the 03-04 conclusions, and from 05 onward run in standard mode (05/06 still confirmed; 07-09 decided based on the new judgment). Time records already written per batch are **not backfilled** — batch records correctly reflect the actual work window, and cross-task statistics can be recognized by the "Small-requirement mode batch" prefix.

### Step Execution Rules

> Each step follows the **five-part pattern**: start confirmation → record start time → execute → record end time → end confirmation.
>
> - **Start confirmation**: must obtain the user's explicit consent
> - **Time records**: write start/end times into `00-overview.md` accurate to the second using `date "+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"`; backfilling afterwards is forbidden
> - **End confirmation**: present "✅ step complete + core conclusions + duration + next-step overview" → wait for the user to reply agree/pause/adjust
> - **Forbidden** to skip steps automatically without confirmation; **forbidden** to merge start/end into a single question
> - **Small-requirement mode exception**: the start/end confirmations of 03-04 and 07-09 may be merged into a single question ("I'm going to do 03-04, report once when done"), but the deliverable files + time records + Progress check-offs are **not exempt**

### Commit Standards

> This section is the **DEVSOP entry** — `09-commit.md` gives the **checklist + forms**; the complete rules are in the team issue-tracker skill / `SKILL.md` red line 4.

**Order**: ① Ask about the issue/task ticket → ② Release the environment (team environment management Skill) → ③ Advance the ticket status to "Developing" (team issue-tracker Skill) → ④ Write the `09-commit.md` commit message → ⑤ Update `00-overview.md` (triggers **boundary point A**) → ⑥ One-time `git add` (code + plans deliverables + 00-overview.md + docs) → ⑦ `git commit` (first time only) → ⑧ `git push` creates the MR, triggering the ticket status **Developing → CR** → ⑨ (repeatable until the MR merges) code fix amend → merge triggers **boundary point B**.

> **Note on timing**: the trigger condition for the ticket status "Developing → CR" is "automatic after MR submission"; only push (step ⑧) creating the MR can trigger it, and it is **not** a prerequisite of step ③; step ③ only needs to advance to "Developing".
>
> **New: forbidden to modify `00-overview.md` / `09-commit.md` after boundary points A / B** — completing steps ④+⑤ triggers boundary point A (commit content finalized); MR merge triggers boundary point B (task wrap-up). Between the two, the **only exception** is the step ⑨ code fix via amend — **only change the code itself, do not touch md**; repeatable without limit, always one commit; once merged, completely frozen. Full rules in the "1. Execution Order" section of `09-commit.md`.

**When entering commit, you MUST first ask whether there is an issue/task ticket** (AI must execute entry): do not just look at the `00-overview.md` Meta field and assume yes / no; if there is none, you **must guide the user to create one** (default recommended path A: AI creates it on behalf via the team issue-tracker skill). 4 situations: ① user gives an ID ② AI creates it on behalf ③ user creates it manually then gives the ID ④ skip (must record the reason in the key decision log). See the "0.0 Ask about the ticket" section of `09-commit.md`.

**Ticket status advancement** (mandatory when part of the team flow): before commit, call the team issue-tracker Skill to advance the status from the current node to "Developing" (solution reviewed → scheduled → developing); **CR is automatically triggered by the MR submission after push**, not completed before commit, and is **not mandatory** to backfill in `09-commit.md` (the tracker's status is the only source). **Before task wrap-up**, query the real ticket status with the team issue-tracker Skill to confirm it has landed on **CR**. See the "0.2 Ticket Status Advancement" section of `09-commit.md`.

**Format**: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>` + ticket reference footer `--<kind>=<id>` (**default `--story=<id>`**; change to `--bug=<id>` for bug fixes; GitHub-style `#<id>` also accepted; CI validation regex `--(bug|story|task|test|other)=\d+` or `#\d+`, overridable via `TICKET_FOOTER_PATTERN`).

**One MR one commit (iron rule)**: the MR for this task may only have one commit. Any fix (before push / follow-up after DEVSOP completes / push meta-information additions) must go through `git commit --amend` to accumulate into the original commit; **strictly forbidden** to add a second commit. After amend, push must use `git push --force-with-lease` (**forbidden** bare `--force`). See the "2. Amend Process" section of `09-commit.md`.

